## Voice

- Prefer Azure Neural TTS `en-GB-SoniaNeural` (uksouth) for current cuts. Coral OpenAI remains on older V1 archives.
- Say **adviser**, not advisor. Say **Agreement in Principle** in full, never “AIP”.
- Say **Mortgage Easy** in VO (two words). On-screen brand is **MortgageEasy**.
- Do not stretch with `atempo` to fit picture. Lock picture to transcribed speech.
- Do not burn captions into the MP4. Site captions are HTML/VTT, shown only while muted.

## Picture

- Native speed only. Never freeze or slow-mo talking heads. Do not loop talking-head clips.
- Still → image-to-video invents new people. For reverse angles of an existing take, use **Aleph video-to-video** from the locked clip, with face keyframes when faces were not in frame.
- **Family lock:** husband = olive-brown skin, short dark curls, olive shirt over white tee. Wife = cream knit, shoulder-length brown hair. Two children in family scenes. Adviser = ~50, greying, navy blazer, light blue shirt.
- MortgageEasy **white tablet badge** (`protect-gfx/badge-protect.png`, native size at 20:16) on branded live shots. Navy open/close credit uses `open-logo.png` centred — no corner badge.
- Final export: Constrained Baseline, no B-frames, `setpts=N/24/TB`, stereo AAC, `+faststart`.

## Site player

- Muted autoplay on scroll into view. Captions along the bottom while muted; hide them when unmuted.
- End card: **Start your journey** → `#your-journey`.
- Do not show a Draft badge on live films.
